<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="080" project="record-header-and-notepad-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Migrate Matter to Spaarke Record Header — re-bind + parity regression QA vs the task-002 baseline</title>
    <phase>5 Rollout</phase>
    <gate>blocked — startable when 002, 034 and 070 are ✅ (parity baseline captured; control shipped; waves 1-3 complete)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Operator/maker configuration + QA task — no .cs/.ts/.tsx files are modified. The pcf tag denotes the control under test, not code implementation, so the tag-based FULL trigger is deliberately overridden per plan.md Phase 5. The weight of this task is in QA judgment, which is why it carries an opus model-tier despite STANDARD rigor.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Parity regression judgment: assessing a screenshot diff against the task-002 baseline with a deliberate intended-change carve-out (lookup interaction), and issuing the go/no-go that gates the IRREVERSIBLE task 081 retirement. High blast radius of a wrong call.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Operator/maker task in the live spaarkedev1 environment; Matter migrates LAST by design (it is the parity regression test). Runs alone as its own wave.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>002, 034, 070</deps>
    <tags>pcf, dataverse, config, deploy, migration</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Re-bind the Matter (sprk_matter) main form from the old MatterHeaderPcf control to the new Spaarke Record
    Header, reproducing R1 v1.0.20's exact 5-field layout, then run the parity regression QA against the
    task-002 baseline — light AND dark. Your go/no-go verdict gates task 081, the irreversible retirement.

    ⚠️ UPDATED 2026-08-27: the lookup-exclusion carve-out this task previously carried is **WITHDRAWN**.
    FR-15a was amended — the header now renders the SAME shared inline `components/LookupField` that R1's
    MatterHeader already renders, so parity is assessed UNQUALIFIED. See the baseline caveat below.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform operator/maker with Dataverse form-designer access to spaarkedev1. Follow ADRs strictly.
    Expertise: model-driven-app form configuration, regression QA judgment, screenshot-diff assessment.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The "Matter main form" (4fa382f2-c273-f011-b4cb-6045bdd6a665) renders the new Spaarke Record Header
    identically to the task-002 v1.0.20 baseline (lookup interaction excepted); all R1 live-QA behaviours are
    confirmed to survive; the parity verdict (explicit GO / NO-GO for task 081) plus evidence is recorded in
    projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/matter-parity-qa.md. The old control remains in the
    environment untouched — its deletion is task 081.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Matter migrates LAST because it is the strongest regression test (spec FR-26; design §8). The parity
      target is the task-002 baseline artifact, NOT the live current state — the shipped v1.0.20 header is
      currently broken by RS-1 (its $select names the deleted sprk_mattersummary column → HTTP 400; spec
      FR-23). R2 fixes that by construction: the new control's sparkle reads sprk_recordsummary. Owner decision
      D-4: MatterHeaderPcf retires on delivery with NO dormant-release window — the ONLY rollback window is
      between this task and task 081 (re-add the old control to the field's control list; instant, no
      redeploy). This task's pixel-parity QA is what earns closing that window.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/ (task-002 baseline artifact — screenshots light+dark, exact 5-field layout + spans, bound field, footer version)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/record-header-and-notepad-r1/notes/matter-form-binding-instructions.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/design.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/RecordHeaderConfiguration.ts</file>
      <file role="new">projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/matter-parity-qa.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="002" status="pending">MatterHeaderPcf v1.0.20 parity baseline — the diff target; without it there is nothing to compare against</dependency>
      <dependency task="034" status="pending">Completed RecordHeader PCF importable as the RecordHeaderPcf solution</dependency>
      <dependency task="070" status="pending">Waves 1-3 (Project, WA, Invoice, Event, Agreement) bound and accepted</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">FR-25 scope: re-bind ONLY the "Matter main form" 4fa382f2-c273-f011-b4cb-6045bdd6a665 — NEVER the legacy "Information" form.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT delete, remove from the environment, or otherwise retire the old MatterHeaderPcf control in this task — that is task 081's prescriptive two-step procedure. This task only removes the old control from the sprk_matternumber field's control list on the main form; the control itself stays importable/re-addable as the rollback path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Parity is assessed UNQUALIFIED (spec criterion 15, updated 2026-08-27). Both controls now render the same shared inline `components/LookupField`, so the former lookup-interaction exclusion no longer applies. ⚠️ BUT: the shared component was upgraded on 2026-08-27 (right-side browse button, overlaying dropdown, thin scrollbar, pinned Advanced). If the task-002 baseline was captured from a MatterHeaderPcf build that PREDATES that upgrade, its lookups will differ — rebuild + redeploy MatterHeaderPcf and re-capture the baseline, or the diff will blame this migration for a shared-library change. Confirm which build the baseline came from BEFORE diffing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">This task modifies form configuration and QA notes only. If parity QA surfaces a code defect, do NOT patch code inside this task — record it, STOP, and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Parity is assessed in BOTH light and dark themes; high contrast is spot-checked (NFR-03).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NFR-01/NFR-02 are measured THIS WAVE: bundle ≤250 KB minified, TTI ≤300 ms warm / ≤800 ms cold on the Matter form.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NFR-07: the Notepad/SmartTodo launch contracts are byte-identical external API — verify, never alter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NFR-09: form and record GUIDs are environment data — acceptable in notes only, never in any shipped artifact.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Matter migration + parity regression QA</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ui-test/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/control-initialization.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/fluent-v9-modern-theming.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Maker binding recipe (proven in R1)" location="projects/record-header-and-notepad-r1/notes/matter-form-binding-instructions.md">
        The re-bind follows this recipe with one addition (design §8 step 3): REMOVE the old control from sprk_matternumber's control list before adding "Spaarke Record Header".
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Context + rigor declaration. Verify 002, 034 and 070 are ✅. Locate and load the task-002 baseline artifact — if it is missing or incomplete, STOP (there is no parity target).</step>
    <step order="1">Author the Matter layoutJson reproducing the EXACT 5-field layout from the task-002 baseline. Expected shape (baseline wins on any conflict):
{ "_version": "1.0", "title": "Matter", "columns": 3,
  "fields": [
    { "name": "sprk_matternumber", "span": 1, "required": true },
    { "name": "sprk_mattername", "span": 2 },
    { "name": "sprk_mattertype", "span": 1 },
    { "name": "sprk_practicearea", "span": 1 },
    { "name": "sprk_matterdescription", "span": 3 } ] }
(summaryField omitted deliberately — defaults to sprk_recordsummary via RECORDSUMMARY_FIELD, per the FR-22 standardization.) Verify against the shipped RecordHeaderConfiguration v1.0 types before pasting.</step>
    <step order="2">make.powerapps.com → Solutions → Tables → sprk_matter → Forms → "Matter main form" (4fa382f2-c273-f011-b4cb-6045bdd6a665) — NEVER the legacy "Information" form → ⋯ → Edit form → Edit in classic.</step>
    <step order="3">Click sprk_matternumber → Controls tab → REMOVE the old "Matter Header" control from the field's control list (do NOT delete the control from the environment) → Add Control → "Spaarke Record Header" → Add → tick Web (and Phone/Tablet) → re-enter Bound field / Header title / Show version footer → paste the layoutJson as a static value.</step>
    <step order="4">Save → Publish. Confirm the swap took via the version footer (the in-UI check that the NEW control is rendering, design §8 step 4).</step>
    <step order="5">Parity QA against the task-002 baseline on the same Matter record(s) the baseline used: screenshot diff in LIGHT and DARK, field-by-field (labels, values, spans, typography, spacing, toolbar). EXCLUDE the lookup interaction from the diff (OOB picker vs inline dropdown — intended, FR-15a). Record every observed difference and classify it: intended (FR-15a lookup; FR-22 sparkle source) vs regression.</step>
    <step order="6">Confirm R1's live-QA behaviours survive: (a) inline edit stages to the form buffer, form goes dirty, NO re-render flash, form Save persists; (b) Notepad opens in the 25% × 35% modal scoped to the record; (c) To Do opens SmartTodo with the openTodos filter (action=openTodos&amp;regardingType=sprk_matter&amp;regardingId=…); (d) dark AND high-contrast theming; (e) sparkle popover renders (reads sprk_recordsummary — "No summary yet" where empty); (f) Matter Type + Practice Area render correct values and the OOB picker resolves them with zero hard-coded constants (LOOKUP_META deleted — spec criterion 16).</step>
    <step order="7">Run the standard negative QA: malformed ({{{) and absent layoutJson each degrade to derived defaults; a configured field not on the form fails loudly on edit.</step>
    <step order="8">Wave measurement: bundle.js bytes after npm run build:prod; TTI cold + warm on the Matter form.</step>
    <step order="9">Write projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/matter-parity-qa.md: baseline reference, light+dark diff evidence, intended-difference register, R1-behaviour checklist, measurements, and an EXPLICIT "GO for task 081" or "NO-GO" verdict. Task 081 must not start without a recorded GO.</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="11">Document any deviation in projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If parity vs the task-002 baseline fails on ANYTHING other than the lookup interaction (the FR-15a OOB-picker change is the only spec-sanctioned exclusion), STOP — record NO-GO, do NOT proceed to task 081, and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6. The rollback window (re-add the old control to the field's control list) exists ONLY while 081 has not run.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any R1 live-QA behaviour (form-buffer dirty state without flash, 25%×35% Notepad modal, openTodos SmartTodo filter, dark/high-contrast theming) does not survive, STOP — record NO-GO and escalate; do not patch code inside this task.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the task-002 baseline artifact is missing or too incomplete to diff against, STOP and escalate — do not substitute memory or the live (RS-1-broken) v1.0.20 rendering as the parity target.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Parity vs task-002 baseline (light + dark)">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_matter&amp;id={baseline-record-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Open the same Matter record used by the task-002 baseline</step>
        <step>Capture screenshots light and dark; diff against the baseline field-by-field (labels, values, spans, typography, spacing, toolbar, footer)</step>
        <step>Include the lookup cells in the diff — the exclusion was withdrawn 2026-08-27. First confirm the baseline came from a MatterHeaderPcf build that includes the 2026-08-27 shared-LookupField upgrade; if not, re-capture it.</step>
        <step>Check the console for JavaScript errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Renders identically to the baseline, lookups included; no console errors (spec criterion 15)</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="R1 behaviours survive">
      <steps>
        <step>Edit sprk_mattername inline — form goes dirty with NO re-render flash; form Save persists; refresh confirms</step>
        <step>Click Notepad — 25% × 35% modal scoped to this Matter</step>
        <step>Click To Do — SmartTodo opens with the openTodos filter for this Matter</step>
        <step>Click the sparkle — popover renders from sprk_recordsummary ("No summary yet" where empty)</step>
        <step>Click Matter Type and Practice Area cells — the INLINE type-ahead dropdown opens under the field (NOT the side pane), the right-side magnifier browses without typing, the pinned Advanced action opens the OOB Xrm.Utility.lookupObjects dialog, there is NO "+ New", and opening the dropdown does not push the fields below it down. Selection stages to the form buffer.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All R1 live-QA behaviours intact; launch contracts byte-identical (NFR-07)</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Config degradation (negative paths)">
      <steps>
        <step>With layoutJson = {{{ : console.warn + derived defaults, never blank, never thrown</step>
        <step>With layoutJson absent: derived defaults render</step>
        <step>With a layout field not on the form: attempted edit throws "Field '…' not on form"</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Graceful degradation (NFR-10); loud failure on missing form field (FR-14)</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode + High Contrast Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode; verify the full header (fields, toolbar, popover, modals) adapts with semantic tokens</step>
        <step>Diff dark-mode rendering against the task-002 DARK baseline</step>
        <step>Spot-check high contrast mode</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Dark parity holds vs baseline; all colors are Fluent v9 semantic tokens (ADR-021 / NFR-03)</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="browser">make.powerapps.com classic form designer + live-record QA + screenshot capture (ui-test skill / Chrome integration)</tool>
    <tool name="pac">Solution verification (pac solution list)</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Bundle measurement via npm run build:prod in the RecordHeader PCF folder</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/matter-parity-qa.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The Matter main form renders the NEW Spaarke Record Header (version footer confirms the swap) with the exact 5-field baseline layout; the old control is removed from the field's control list but still present in the environment (rollback intact until 081).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Screenshot diff vs the task-002 baseline passes in LIGHT and DARK with the lookup interaction as the ONLY unclassified-as-regression difference (spec criterion 15); every other observed difference is either absent or explicitly classified as intended (FR-15a lookup / FR-22 sparkle source) in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">R1 behaviours survive: form-buffer dirty state with no re-render flash; 25% × 35% Notepad modal; openTodos SmartTodo filter; dark AND high-contrast theming (design §8).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Matter Type + Practice Area render and resolve via metadata with LOOKUP_META deleted — grep for LOOKUP_META returns nothing, and both lookups work functionally (spec criterion 16).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Sparkle reads sprk_recordsummary and renders "No summary yet" where empty — no reference to the deleted sprk_mattersummary anywhere in the header path (FR-22/FR-23 RS-1 fixed by construction).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: malformed AND absent layoutJson degrade to derived defaults; a configured field not on the form fails loudly on edit (spec criteria 5-6).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Bundle ≤250 KB minified and TTI ≤300 ms warm / ≤800 ms cold measured this wave on the Matter form (spec criteria 8-9).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/matter-parity-qa.md exists with baseline reference, light+dark evidence, the intended-difference register, measurements, and an EXPLICIT GO / NO-GO verdict for task 081.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec refs: FR-22, FR-23 (RS-1), FR-25, FR-26, Success Criteria 1-9 + 15 + 16; design §8 (migration
    sequence + rollback) and §5.2 (the Matter layout shape). The parity TARGET is the task-002 baseline
    artifact, not the live v1.0.20 rendering — the shipped control is currently RS-1-broken (HTTP 400 on
    load). One expected non-visual difference beyond the lookup: the sparkle's backing column is now
    sprk_recordsummary (v1.0.20 read the deleted sprk_mattersummary), so popover CONTENT may differ on any
    record the baseline captured with old summary text — classify under FR-22 as intended, with the evidence
    noted. Rollback: between this task and 081 only — re-add the old control to sprk_matternumber's control
    list (instant, no redeploy). Owner decision D-4: no dormant-release window after delivery.
  </notes>

